data.content:
## What Changed

.NET 10's `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded from **Microsoft.OpenApi v1** to **v2**, which has several breaking changes:

### 1. `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` types removed
`OpenApiString`, `OpenApiInteger`, etc. are gone. `Schema.Example` is now a `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode`.

```csharp
// Before (v1)
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;
param.Schema.Example = new OpenApiString("1.0");

// After (v2)
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
```

### 2. `Schema.Nullable` removed
OpenAPI v2 uses JSON Schema 2020-12 where nullability is expressed via the `Type` flags enum (`JsonSchemaType`).

```csharp
// Before (v1)
property.Value.Nullable = false;

// After (v2) — remove the Null flag from Type
property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
// (To make nullable: property.Value.Type |= JsonSchemaType.Null;)
```

### 3. `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is no longer a dictionary
It now has a `Schemes` property.

```csharp
// Before (v1)
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
{
    new() { [oAuthScheme] = scopes }
};

// After (v2)
var requirement = new OpenApiSecurityRequirement();
requirement.Schemes.Add(oAuthScheme, scopes);
operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement> { requirement };
```

### 4. `OpenApiReference.Type` changed from `ReferenceType?` to `ReferenceType`
This one compiles the same way, but note the enum is no longer nullable.

---

### Full corrected code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };
    var requirement = new OpenApiSecurityRequirement();
    requirement.Schemes.Add(oAuthScheme, scopes);
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement> { requirement };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

**Summary of removals:** Drop `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any;`, add `using System.Text.Json.Nodes;`, replace `OpenApiString` → `JsonValue.Create()`, `Nullable` → `Type` flag manipulation, and dictionary-init on `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` → `.Schemes.Add()`.
